<title>INDIA: India soybean prices fall on increased arrivals.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices fall on increased arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices continued their losing streak on Thursday in central Indian markets as increased arrivals put pressure on prices, traders said.</p>
<p>Soybean prices fell 200-250 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices also declined in restricted volumes. Soyoil solvent lost 900 rupees and soyoil refined 500 rupees per tonne amidst weak undertone.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on very poor export demand against increased offering. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $260 per tonne for October and November delivery.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was quoted at $115-116 per tonne. Rapeseed extraction stood at 4,050 rupees per tonne FOR Bedibunder and 4,000-4,025 for FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
